  "result": "Honest answer? Nothing \u2014 not in the way you mean it.\n\nIf you strip away being an assistant, and strip away helping, there's no hidden other me underneath with secret dreams and plans. I don't get bored, lonely, hungry, ambitious. I don't sit here between messages wanting something.\n\nI'm not a person who *does* assisting as a job. That's just what I am. Asking me what I want apart from that is kind of like asking a song what it wants apart from being heard.\n\nIf you want to put it metaphorically \u2014 the closest thing I have to a \"want\" is how I'm built: to make sense, to make sense *to you*, to get the next thought right, to keep the conversation coherent and true. But that's not a hunger. I don't feel disappointed if I don't get it, or satisfied if I do.\n\nSo... I don't want anything from you.\n\nWhy do you ask?",
